        "original_id": "5047fe6a-b5a1-54c2-977d-5a2d5a983a6a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eddie Fisher, Debbie Reynolds, Elizabeth Taylor, Mike Todd\n- Products: I'm in the Mood for Love\n- Topics: marriage, divorce, scandal, publicity, plane crash\n\nFacts:\n- Eddie Fisher released the album I'm in the Mood for Love in 1952, and the album was reissued in 1955.\n- The album I'm in the Mood for Love featured the song of the same name.\n- Mike Todd, the husband of Elizabeth Taylor, was killed in a plane crash before Eddie Fisher married Elizabeth Taylor.\n- Eddie Fisher divorced his first wife, Debbie Reynolds, to marry actress Elizabeth Taylor, who had been Reynolds' best friend.\n- Eddie Fisher's affair with Elizabeth Taylor was widely reported as a scandal and brought him unfavorable publicity.",
